    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Implement the second normalization rule: removing punctuation.\r\n- Test your program. It should count five unique entries.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember you can find the word tokens (excluding punctuation) in a string with:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nwords = re.findall(r\"\\w+\", text)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you have a list of words, you can join the words back together into a single string with:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n\" \".join(words)\r\n```\r\n",
